{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_16", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat bench/programs/Makefile test/cosim/reference.py'", "aggregated_output": "CROSS   := riscv32-unknown-elf\nCC      := $(CROSS)-gcc\n\n# CoreMark build knobs. Defaults are the canonical EEMBC reporting config\n# (2K data size, -O3); tools/eval/fpga.py's COREMARK_EXPECTED CRCs assume\n# exactly these defaults.\n# - COREMARK_SIZE: TOTAL_DATA_SIZE in coremark.h (#ifndef-guarded). 2000 is\n#   the EEMBC canonical reporting config (used by VexRiscv et al.); 6000\n#   makes the matrix/list/state working sets ~3x larger so the score is\n#   harder to inflate via register-resident working sets.\n# - COREMARK_OPT: gcc optimization. -O3 is the standard CoreMark publication\n#   flag; -O2 is what the V0 baseline used.\n# Defaults match VexRiscv's published CoreMark methodology so the\n# orchestrator's fitness number is directly comparable to public CoreMark\n# results. To override (e.g. for the prior 6K -O2 V0 baseline):\n#     make bench/programs/coremark.elf COREMARK_SIZE=6000 COREMARK_OPT=-O2\nCOREMARK_SIZE ?= 2000\nCOREMARK_OPT  ?= -O3\n\nCFLAGS  := -march=rv32im -mabi=ilp32 $(COREMARK_OPT) -static -nostartfiles \\\n           -specs=nano.specs -specs=nosys.specs \\\n           -T bench/programs/link.ld -Ibench/programs/coremark \\\n           -Ibench/programs/coremark/baremetal \\\n           -DTOTAL_DATA_SIZE=$(COREMARK_SIZE)\n\nSRCS := bench/programs/coremark/core_list_join.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_main.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_matrix.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_state.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_util.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/core_portme.c \\\n        bench/programs/crt0.S\n\nbench/programs/coremark.elf: $(SRCS)\n\t$(CC) $(CFLAGS) $^ -o $@\n\nbench/programs/selftest.elf: bench/programs/selftest.S\n\t$(CC) -march=rv32im -mabi=ilp32 -static -nostartfiles \\\n\t  -T bench/programs/link.ld $< -o $@\n\n# Random full-trace programs (V2). The .S files are generated once by\n# gen_random_trace.py <seed> and committed, so every candidate runs the\n# same programs.\nRANDOM_ELFS := bench/programs/random1.elf bench/programs/random2.elf bench/programs/random3.elf\n\nbench/pro\n…[12681 of 15753 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e91b5b051168e433]…\nrap_kwargs, wrd=rd, wval=(pc + 4) & MASK)\n\n        if op == 0x37:  # LUI\n            return self._retire(**trap_kwargs, wrd=rd, wval=imm_u & MASK)\n\n        if op == 0x17:  # AUIPC\n            return self._retire(**trap_kwargs, wrd=rd, wval=(pc + imm_u) & MASK)\n\n        if op == 0x0F:  # MISC-MEM (FENCE / FENCE.I) — architectural NOP\n            return self._retire(**trap_kwargs)\n\n        if op == 0x73:  # SYSTEM\n            if instr == 0x00100073:\n                return self._retire(**trap_kwargs)\n            return self._retire(**trap_kwargs, trap=1)\n\n        # Unknown opcode (AMO 0x2F, etc.) — DUT decoder default-illegal.\n        return self._retire(**trap_kwargs, trap=1)\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    cpu = RV32IM()\n    cpu.load_elf(sys.argv[1])\n    max_insns = int(sys.argv[2]) if len(sys.argv) > 2 else 10_000_000\n    import json\n    for _ in range(max_insns):\n        r = cpu.step()\n        if r is None:\n            break\n        print(json.dumps(r))\n        if r['insn'] == 0x00100073:\n            break\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
